Theorem RL-28: unknown callees order all pending ownership events

  Preconditions:
    - The call is FFI, indirect, or otherwise lacks a trusted contract.

  Soundness property:
    Every pending logical ownership event is ordered before an unknown call.
    A known contract delegates to RL-27 selective ordering. The theorem does
    not prescribe a worklist flush or physical counter operation.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate FFI, indirect, no-contract Apply, and known-contract cases.
    Coverage gate: 4 cases; an unknown callee may never skip ordering.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl28_unknown_callee_event_ordering)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-28 conservatively orders all pending logical ownership events before every unknown call
